Subject: KRT: Add the krt_tunnel route attribute

A filter sets krt_tunnel to the name of a tunnel device. The kernel
protocol then programs the route through that device, on-link, with the
BGP next hop as the gateway. Calico uses this for IP-in-IP routes.

The attribute is a string, so this adds a string extended attribute type.
A route already in the kernel is compared by its tunnel device when the
attribute is set, and by gateway and interface otherwise.

Squashed from these projectcalico/bird commits, oldest first. Each keeps
its author and message.

